  "details": "Before disabled objects did not network anything and attempting to set ownership would queue the ownership request when the object was reactivated.\n\nNow disabled objects can be set ownership and network events despite being disabled.\n\nSynced variables do not update until the object is activated (expected).\n\nDisabling an object was a secure way of saving network bandwidth and ensuring no networking can occur locally on that object.\n\nHere is a video of the current behavior: https://1drv.ms/v/c/907a50bc9a229edf/EcEJD7U8gXlHoO5PXgEuFpIBNwmgXti4WPBeTZht3j9TRQ?e=yPcxKw",
